invariant: INV-10
file: record.c
catches: aes_suite_test_extern
reason: rec_seal seals an AES-GCM record at REC_AES_GCM_RECORDS_MAX, a record
  past what one key may seal under RFC 9846 section 5.5. ch_write never
  asks it to, so only the record layer's own boundary test sees the rule
  go.

--- old
    if (suite_runs_aes_gcm(d->suite) && d->seq >= REC_AES_GCM_RECORDS_MAX) {
--- new
    if (suite_runs_aes_gcm(d->suite) && d->seq > REC_AES_GCM_RECORDS_MAX) {
